tand why but he still goes to and see strange things as if he was meant to witness them.</span><br /> <br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1540,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","user":"Basic","date":". 07-27-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:34:06-07:00","id":1123014,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><u><b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Benjamin C. Weiser</span></b></u></span><br /> Benjamin's most of his life working in the store. A shop called the Wandering Eye. It's been in his family before he was even a glimmer in his father's eye. It was not till his teens that he was showed that the store works as a video archive for the network. From a young age he was taught how to curate and store all this knowledge. The only problem is Benjamin wanted more than to just be a simple curator and protector over the archive. He has not only the urge to create but a god given talent for art of cinematography. While his father and mother trained him to protect the store He would create films with his childhood friends and school mates. His films gained so much traction online that he went full bore into movie directing. He thought he could use this as a way to escape ending up being just a curator like his parents wanted. Even though it hurt his mother and father let him go and pursue his dreams. In Hollywood. For the next decade he followed his dreams in Hollywood directing, producing and writing roughly a whopping 162 films. Movie critics called him a force of nature. Then in the middle of filming a movie c