d a lot with local government to try and improve school conditions.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\"><b>RP Advice: </b>Jason is a very kind man who will do anything for children even he has to go hungry. When speaks he always sounds like he's thinking about what he's saying.</span><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-28T18:24:24-07:00","id":1230969,"title":"","content":"<b><span style=\"font-size:20px\">Elizabeth B. Shoffner </span></b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:Calibri\">Elizabeth family is a upper middle class family that helped settle parts of California and they took lots of pride in it. They even though the bills weighted on them they raised each one of their children like they were aristocracy. Paying for classes on how to act in high class society. In the hopes, their children would elevate the family name. From a young age, Elizabeth was seen as exceptionally beautiful. Just as her older siblings were used to further her family's interests. So was Elizabeth used, at a young age she was given the best classes and training her family could afford. They pressured her and pushed her hard to be the best which got her into an ivy language college like her older brothers and sisters. Even away from home at college, she could not escape the pressure of her family as she worked hard and just as they wanted she graduated at the top of her class but it did not end there before she was even out the door. She got a job at a top fortune 500 tech company working as their head system architect. She s